// Program 3: Call a function with too few arguments.

fun add(a, b) {
    return a + b;
}

print add(5);

// Expected:
// I wondered if the missing argument b might automatically become nil.

// Actual:
// Lox gives a runtime error.

// Why:
// Lox requires the number of arguments in a function call to match
// the number of parameters the function expects.
// add() expects 2 arguments, but only 1 was provided.